    <string name="perm_lan_body">Finds your sensor on your Wi-Fi so syncing is faster. Bluetooth works without it.</string>
    <string name="perm_lan_settings_title">Local network is off</string>
    <string name="perm_lan_settings_body">Turn on local network access for opensensor.space in settings. Bluetooth keeps working.</string>
    <string name="perm_continue">Continue</string>
    <string name="perm_open_settings">Open settings</string>

    <!-- Info sheets -->
    <string name="info_connect_title">Connect a sensor</string>
    <string name="info_connect_body1">Turn on your sensor and keep this phone close. It appears here in a few seconds.</string>
    <string name="info_connect_body2">On the first connection Android asks for a 6 digit code. Read it on the sensor screen. A sensor without a screen uses the PIN its owner set over USB.</string>
    <string name="info_privacy">Bluetooth and your local Wi-Fi reach only your own sensors. No account, no analytics, no location and no uploads. Your files stay on this phone unless you share them.</string>
    <string name="info_collect_body">Collects from your known sensors over Wi-Fi when this phone holds their token, otherwise over Bluetooth. Up to two run at once with a notification, so you can leave the app. Sensors with an open connection are skipped.</string>
    <string name="info_now_body">A 10 second snapshot from the sensor, not a daily average. The face, the word and the colour all show the same band.</string>
    <string name="info_wifi_body">The sensor joins your Wi-Fi so this phone can sync without Bluetooth.</string>
    <string name="info_pairing_body">How a phone proves it is allowed to connect.</string>
    <string name="info_history_body1">Averages use only readings the sensor marked valid, warmed up, fresh and without error.</string>
    <string name="info_history_body2">Coverage is the share of the window with such readings. Three readings in an hour is 1 percent, not an hourly average.</string>
    <string name="info_history_body3">Dashed stretches were logged before the sensor had a clock. Their time is estimated from a later time set on the same power on.</string>
    <string name="info_history_body4">Earlier station readings stay available after a device reset.</string>
    <string name="info_settings_body1">The detail level changes only what you see. Every level reads the same data, and nothing is hidden from the archive or the export.</string>
    <string name="info_settings_body2">Smart Sync never rewrites raw files. Finalizing buffered rows stays a separate confirmed action.</string>
    <string name="info_file_chart_body">One column per synced file in file order. Faint columns have few valid readings, for example during warm up. Dashed columns have an estimated time. Touch a column to read its file, rows, time span and mean.</string>

